{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":"cli","result":{"worker":{"name":"research-iso2-e7a1c4","session_id":"baf450a3-80d9-4a98-aa64-8d511fe75ed1","thread_id":"01a0f31e-88b3-76e3-9451-27b23404960c","cwd":"/private/tmp/cw-iso-e7a1c4/work2","tier":"medium","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","effort":"medium","access":"read_only","attach":{"listener":"ws://127.0.0.1:4611","thread_id":"01a0f31e-88b3-76e3-9451-27b23404960c","attach_command":"codex --remote ws://127.0.0.1:4611","resume_command":"codex --remote ws://127.0.0.1:4611 resume 01a0f31e-88b3-76e3-9451-27b23404960c"},"config":{"web_search":"live"}},"turn":{"turn_id":"01a0f31e-88e9-7663-b53f-56a01eaa978c","status":"completed","error":null},"messages":[{"type":"agent_message","item_id":"msg_0039a7b12b2dea91016abd3725976487d2b79895cbc600f91c","phase":"final_answer","selection":"explicit_final","text":"- **EU:** L-theanine produced by microbial fermentation was determined to be a **novel food**; it therefore needs EU novel-food authorisation before marketing for that production route. [European Commission consultation determination](https://food.ec.europa.eu/document/download/1e468cb7-af61-4aa2-8d4f-976f9783dbae_en?filename=novel-food_consult-status_l-teanina.pdf)\n\n- **United States (FDA GRAS):** FDA issued \u201cno questions\u201d letters for several L-theanine GRAS notices, including chemically synthesised L-theanine (GRN 501); this means FDA did not question the notifier\u2019s GRAS conclusion, rather than granting an FDA approval. [FDA GRAS Notice inventory](https://www.hfpappexternal.fda.gov/scripts/fdcc/index.cfm?cat=&order=DESC&search=l-theanine&set=GRASNotices&sort=GRN_No&startrow=1&type=basic)\n\n- **Japan:** L-theanine is a **designated food additive** under the Food Sanitation Act framework (listed as item 263) and is used as a flavour enhancer/seasoning. [MHLW Food Sanitation Act Enforcement Regulations](https://www.mhlw.go.jp/web/t_doc?dataId=78332000&dataType=0&pageNo=3)\n\n- **Australia (TGA):** Theanine/L-theanine is a **permitted ingredient for listed medicines**, subject to TGA compositional requirements. [TGA compositional guideline](https://www.tga.gov.au/resources/resources/compositional-guidelines/theanine)\n\n- **Canada:** For foods, Health Canada considers L-theanine **non-novel up to 23 mg/day**; separately, it is an accepted medicinal ingredient in natural health products, with higher doses potentially regarded as therapeutic. [Health Canada L-theanine food guidance](https://www.canada.ca/en/health-canada/services/food-nutrition/supplemented-foods/list-permitted-food-ingredients/information-ingredients-foods/information-l-theanine.html)\n\n- **China:** Tea-derived theanine (**\u8336\u53f6\u8336\u6c28\u9178**) is an approved **new food ingredient**, limited to \u22640.4 g/day and excluding infant foods. This approval is issued by the National Health Commission\u2014not NMPA, which regulates drugs and medical devices. [NHC Announcement No. 15 (2014)](https://www.nhc.gov.cn/sps/c100088/201407/9bceee42235d4dcc934ddf3b3e580877.shtml)"}],"structured_output":null,"metrics":{"wall_duration_seconds":{"value":67.12913741599186,"source":"codex-worker","availability":"measured"},"item_counts":{"value":{"userMessage":1,"reasoning":8,"agentMessage":3,"commandExecution":2,"webSearch":5},"source":"codex-worker","availability":"derived"},"command_count":{"value":2,"source":"codex-worker","availability":"derived"},"command_duration_ms":{"value":0,"source":"codex","availability":"derived"},"token_usage":{"value":null,"source":"codex","availability":"unavailable"}},"recovery":{"status":"codex-worker status --name research-iso2-e7a1c4","messages":"codex-worker messages --name research-iso2-e7a1c4","interrupt":"codex-worker interrupt --name research-iso2-e7a1c4","raw_resume":"codex --remote ws://127.0.0.1:4611 resume 01a0f31e-88b3-76e3-9451-27b23404960c"}}}
